# Local testing
- Start test servers with OTP logging and a separate port, so no real SMS is sent (the dev database may have Message Central selected; real SMS went out once):
  ```bash
  cd apps/api && OTP_PROVIDER=log PORT=4100 nohup pnpm exec tsx src/server.ts > ~/.cache/grocery-build/api-test.log 2>&1 &
  ```
- Stop every server you started before finishing (`pkill -f "tsx src/server.ts"`, then check with `pgrep`).
- Seed accounts: `admin@grocery.test` and `staff@grocery.test`, password `grocery-dev`. Customer `+919000000002`, partner `+919000000004` (OTP in the API log).
- WSL memory is limited: run one heavy build at a time (Next.js build, Docker build) and write logs to `~/.cache/grocery-build/`, not `/tmp` (WSL restarts wipe it).

# Deploying and building apps
Follow `docs/deployment.md` (runbook and the table of current clients). The rules that must not be skipped:
- Deploy only what the developer has pushed; the server pulls from GitHub.
- Before deploying, check the deployed commit and read every pending migration (`git diff --name-only <deployed>..origin/main -- apps/api/prisma/migrations`). If one moves data, drops columns or adds `NOT NULL`, check it against the live data and run an on-demand backup first.
- After deploying, confirm `docker compose ps` is healthy and `/health` is `ok`.
- Update every client's server before handing out new app builds.
- Each client is isolated: never reuse secrets between clients, never point one client's app at another's API.
- App builds: per-client values go in that client's `eas.json` profiles and `brands/<brand>/`, never in the shared EAS environments. `APP_ID` is permanent once published; never change it for a published app. Never delete EAS credentials (signing keys). Submit with `--id <build id>`, never `--latest`.

# Production VPS (test client "moozy")
- Connect with `ssh grocery-vps` (key-based, `deploy` user with passwordless sudo). The stack is in `~/moozy/deploy`; domains are `api.moozy.in` and `admin.moozy.in`.
- Deploy after the developer pushes (and, with `IMAGE_PREFIX` set on the server, after CI has built the images):
  ```bash
  ssh grocery-vps '~/moozy/deploy/update.sh'
  ```
  Building on the server (no `IMAGE_PREFIX`) takes about 5 minutes on 1 CPU. Don't poll it repeatedly; check once with `docker compose ps`.
- API tests: `pnpm test` (per-run test database; needs the dev PostgreSQL and Redis). Don't run it alongside a Docker or Next.js build.
- Never print values from `deploy/.env` or `deploy/api.env`; show variable names only. Never ask for passwords in chat.
- Before anything destructive on the server (deleting volumes, data, containers), back up, explain, and get confirmation.
